# File: scripts/__tests__/test-selection.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/test-selection-gate.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/validation-tiers.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-models.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-finalize-verification.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/nmg-sdlc-smoke.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/verification-scope.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/repository-surfaces.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/584-scope-the-pre-merge-gate-s-tests-and-smoke-to-the-change-with-a-claude-selection-checked-by-coverage-and-a-surface-map/requirements.md
Feature: Scope the pre-merge gate's tests and smoke to the change

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Claude selects tests and surfaces for a change
    Given a manifest declaring the top-level selection object and a project snippet routed to gate:selection
    When the pre-merge gate runs for a change
    Then headless Claude receives the rendered prompt, base ref, changed paths, diff and surface ids
    And the opted-in builtin.command validation runs only the selected tests
    And each project provider request carries the changed paths and selected surfaces
    And the artifact selection records the prompt provenance, model, effort, reason, tests and surfaces

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Selection model and effort are configurable
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json declares selection model sonnet and effort high
    When the gate asks Claude for a selection
    Then the call uses sonnet at high
    And without the entry the call uses haiku at xhigh
    And selection effort "huge" fails with the steering/sdlc-models.json diagnostic naming selection.effort

  @SCN003
  Scenario: The command form of selection is rejected
    Given a manifest whose selection is a command with program and args
    When the steering runtime loads it
    Then loading fails with steering_validation_invalid naming selection
    And the message states that selection takes a prompt

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Changed code lines must be covered by the selected tests
    Given a valid steering/test-coverage.json and selected tests that pass
    And a changed executable line that no selected test hits
    When the gate runs the coverage command for the selected tests
    Then the opted-in result records coverage with changedLines, hitLines and uncovered
    And the selection is rejected as selection_uncovered naming the line

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Changed surfaces must be selected
    Given a surfaces map whose surface sources match a changed path
    When Claude's answer omits that surface
    Then the selection is rejected as selection_surface_missing naming the surface
    And an answer with that surface plus an extra surface is accepted

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Surface-bound validations run only for selected surfaces
    Given a project-provider validation bound to a surface
    When the gate runs and the surface is not selected
    Then the validation passes as surface_not_selected without running
    And when the surface is selected the validation runs with the selected surfaces in its request

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Every changed path must be accounted for
    Given a changed path outside the coverage report, the selected surfaces, docPaths and fallbackPaths
    When the gate checks the selection
    Then the selection is rejected as selection_unaccounted naming the path

  @SCN008
  Scenario: A rejected selection escalates to the orchestrator
    Given a gate artifact whose selection is rejected
    When the verify finalizer and the supervised controller process it
    Then the handoff reason is selection_escalation with the escalation details
    And the stage report offers only redispatch and halt and does not route to implement
    And redispatch with guidance reruns verify whose selection prompt contains the guidance and records guidanceSupplied

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Only a docs-only change may select nothing
    Given docPaths globs
    When every changed path matches docPaths and Claude selects nothing
    Then the opted-in validations pass with selection_empty without running and providers receive no surfaces
    And an empty selection for a change with a code path is rejected as selection_empty_code_change

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Full-run fallbacks are kept
    Given a manifest that declares selection
    When a changed path matches fallbackPaths
    Then Claude is not asked and the opted-in validations run in full with fallback_path
    And a failed, timed-out, malformed or all answer runs in full with selection_failed or selection_all
    And providers receive every declared surface

  @SCN011
  Scenario: This repository's smoke runs only the selected surfaces
    Given the smoke validation bound to the interactive command surfaces and execute
    When the selection includes write-spec with a head-bound passed record and not execute
    Then smoke passes listing the write-spec evidence without running a delivery
    And a selected surface without a head-bound record fails as not exercised
    And a selection with execute runs one full provisioned delivery with exact-head merge evidence

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Onboard and upgrade enforce the configuration
    Given a project with a legacy command selection and no surfaces map
    When verification-scope detection runs
    Then it reports a digest-bound verification-scope item listing each finding
    And applying the approved proposal writes selection, surfaces and test coverage configuration
    And a repeat detection proposes nothing

  @SCN013
  Scenario: This repository adopts scoped verification
    Given this repository's steering
    When the repository tests run
    Then every tracked file under workflows, agents, references, commands, hooks and .claude-plugin matches a surface
    And repository.tests opts into selection and steering/test-coverage.json validates
    And verification-scope detection on the repository reports nothing
